' The guide's focus and keys (M12 step 12, L3, L4, D49) as pure functions: a port of MMTVL's GuideModel
' (IPTV/Guide/GuideModel.swift: init :85-104, handle :143-151, the key handlers :244-363, moveRow :369-384,
' moveInGroupPanel :394-409) and the guide part of LiveTVModel.handle (IPTV/LiveTVModel.swift:603-650, Back:
' :675-693). No nodes and no programmes: Roku's TimeGrid moves between programmes itself, so the screen tells this
' model where the grid's focus is (cellIndex, cellCount) and carries out the action that comes back. Uses Lineup,
' so a component that loads this file loads Lineup.bs too.
'
'   open(lineup, lastGroup, focusedChannelID) -> state (MMTVL's GuideModel.init): the remembered group (Lineup's
'     resolvedGroup, so "Teams" reads as "My Teams"), else the default group: the first that isn't My Teams or
'     Antenna, else Antenna, else the first (M7l 8c, M7j L3). When the focused channel isn't in that group, All
'     Channels if there is one, else the channel's own group. The focused channel's row, else row 0.
'   rowsOf(lineup, group) -> the group's rows: { kind: "channel", channelID } per channel; My Teams starts with
'     { kind: "chooseTeams", channelID: "" }. (My Teams' upcoming games, kind "upcoming", come with step 18.)
'   setLineup(state, lineup) -> state after a playlist refresh or a favorites or hiding change (GuideModel.setLineup,
'     GuideModel.swift:183-207): the same group (by name; else the default group), the focused row by its id, else
'     the focused channel's row, else the same row index clamped; a focused group-column row keeps its group by
'     name (else its position, clamped). Focus (grid, channel, groups, search) stays.
'   visibleStart(first, position, count, visible) -> the first row a list of visible rows shows so that position
'     is in view, moving as little as possible from first (GuideModel.keepGroupVisible; also the channel menu's
'     window, LiveMenu): clamped to 0...count - visible.
'   jumpTarget(state) -> where the screen sends TimeGrid for the model's focus: { row, kind }, kind "channel" (the
'     row's channel cell, jumpToChannelInfo) or "grid" (a programme cell, jumpToChannel; also with the column open,
'     which is drawn over the grid). invalid with no rows. The screen keeps it as the pending jump until TimeGrid
'     reports a focus.
'   pendingFor(target, held) -> the pending jump for a jump to target (jumpTarget's): invalid when target is invalid
'     or is held, the cell TimeGrid last reported ({ row, kind }; invalid when unknown, as after new content), since
'     TimeGrid may raise no report for a jump to the cell it holds; else target.
'   gridReport(focus, pending, reported, rebuilding) -> { apply, isInput, pending }: what a TimeGrid focus report
'     means (QA of step 12: a refresh with the column open must not hand the keys to the grid).
'     focus: the model's; pending: the last jumpTarget sent and not yet reported, or invalid; reported: { row, kind },
'     kind "grid" (programFocusedDetails) or "channel" (channelInfoFocused); rebuilding: the screen is replacing
'     TimeGrid's content (a report then is the code's, whatever it says).
'     The pending jump's own report is never input (the code's move doesn't restart the 3-minute timer, D51; MMTVL
'     restarts it on commands) and settles it (pending comes back invalid).
'     With the column open (groups or search), nothing applies: the column keeps its focus and highlight.
'     While rebuilding, only the pending jump's report applies (it agrees with the model); another keeps pending.
'     Else apply (the model takes the report's row and focus), and any report but the pending jump's is the user's.
'   handle(key, press, state) -> { handled, action, state, wrapped }
'     key, press: as PlayerKeys.handle. A release does nothing, handled for the keys a press handles.
'     state  { focus, lineup, groups, groupIndex, groupFocus, rows, row, cellIndex, cellCount, canReturn,
'              isPlaying }
'       focus       "grid" (a programme cell), "channel" (the row's channel cell, M6 L8), "groups" (the group
'                   column) or "search" (the Search row above the groups, M7f L12)
'       groups      lineup.groups; groupIndex: the selected group; groupFocus: the focused one in the column
'       rows        rowsOf(lineup, the selected group); row: the focused row
'       cellIndex   the focused programme cell in the row (0 = the first, the one on now), cellCount its cells
'                   (at least 1: a row with no guide has one placeholder cell). The screen keeps both in step
'                   with TimeGrid; Left on cell 0 goes to the channel cell, Right on the last cell does nothing.
'       canReturn   LiveTVModel.canReturnToChannel: a channel plays, or a failed or stopped one is still in
'                   the playlist. isPlaying: it plays (Back returns without a reconnect).
'     state that comes back is a new object (lineup, groups and rows are shared, never changed).
'     wrapped: a one-step move looped past an end of the rows or the group column (M7n L3, L4: put the rows in
'     place instead of sliding).
'     handled: true for every key in the table below (Back never leaves Live TV, D49), else false.
'     action: { type, ... }: none, play { channelID }, channelMenu { channelID }, groupChanged { group,
'       groupIndex } (remember it as lastGroup), openSearch, openTeamPicker, togglePause (the playing channel,
'       MMTVL's Play/Pause in the guide), returnToChannel { reload } (Back: full screen on the channel; reload when
'       it isn't playing, which retries a failed one), openSettings (step 13: * in the group column, or with no
'       rows at all, as on a first launch with no playlist).
'
' The keys (Roku's on the left; L4 maps Rewind/Fast Forward to MMTVL's Channel Up/Down, which page):
'   up / down          the row (or, in the column, the group) above / below; loops (M7n L3)
'   left               grid: the previous cell, from the first cell the channel cell; channel cell: the groups
'                      (on the selected group); groups / Search: back to the grid
'   right              grid: the next cell; channel cell: the grid; groups: select the group; Search: open Search
'   rewind / channelup     page up: 6 rows (MMTVL's visibleRows), 7 in the column (visibleGroupRows)
'   fastforward / channeldown  page down. A page stops at the end row and wraps only from it.
'   OK                 grid: play; channel cell: the channel menu; groups: select the group; Search: open Search;
'                      Choose Teams: the team picker; an upcoming game: play its channel
'   options            the channel menu (grid or channel cell); Settings in the column (Search or a group) and
'                      when the group has no rows (step 13: MMTVL reaches Settings from Home, which a Roku app
'                      doesn't have); nothing on Choose Teams
'   back               the column or Search: back to the grid; else return to the channel, and with nothing to
'                      return to, nothing (M7m L2, D49)
'   play               togglePause
'   replay             nothing
namespace GuideKeys

    ' MMTVL's GuideModel.visibleRows: a page of rows.
    const pageRows = 6
    ' MMTVL's GuideModel.visibleGroupRows: a page in the group column (Search and the groups).
    const pageGroupRows = 7
    const searchRowGroup = -1

    function open(built as object, lastGroup as dynamic, focusedChannelID = "" as dynamic) as object
        groups = built.groups
        groupIndex = -1
        resolved = Lineup.resolvedGroup(built, lastGroup)
        if GuideKeys.isText(resolved) then groupIndex = GuideKeys.textIndex(groups, resolved)
        if groupIndex < 0 then groupIndex = GuideKeys.defaultGroupIndex(groups)
        rows = GuideKeys.rowsOf(built, GuideKeys.groupName(groups, groupIndex))
        hasFocus = GuideKeys.isText(focusedChannelID) and focusedChannelID <> ""
        if hasFocus and GuideKeys.channelRow(rows, focusedChannelID) < 0
            ' Show the focused channel: All Channels if there is one, else its own group.
            fallback = GuideKeys.textIndex(groups, Lineup.allChannelsGroup)
            if fallback < 0
                for each channel in built.visibleChannels
                    if channel.id = focusedChannelID
                        if GuideKeys.isText(channel.group) then fallback = GuideKeys.textIndex(groups, channel.group)
                        exit for
                    end if
                end for
            end if
            if fallback >= 0
                groupIndex = fallback
                rows = GuideKeys.rowsOf(built, groups[groupIndex])
            end if
        end if
        startRow = 0
        if hasFocus then startRow = GuideKeys.channelRow(rows, focusedChannelID)
        if startRow < 0 then startRow = 0
        return {
            focus: "grid",
            lineup: built,
            groups: groups,
            groupIndex: groupIndex,
            groupFocus: groupIndex,
            rows: rows,
            row: startRow,
            cellIndex: 0,
            cellCount: 1,
            canReturn: false,
            isPlaying: false
        }
    end function

    function rowsOf(built as object, group as dynamic) as object
        rows = []
        if not GuideKeys.isText(group) then return rows
        if group = Lineup.teamsGroup then rows.Push({ kind: "chooseTeams", channelID: "" })
        for each channel in Lineup.channelsIn(built, group)
            rows.Push({ kind: "channel", channelID: channel.id })
        end for
        return rows
    end function

    function handle(key as dynamic, press as dynamic, state as object) as object
        result = { handled: GuideKeys.isKey(key), action: GuideKeys.action("none"), state: GuideKeys.copyState(state), wrapped: false }
        if not result.handled or press <> true then return result
        current = result.state
        if key = "play"
            result.action = GuideKeys.action("togglePause")
            return result
        end if
        if current.focus = "groups" or current.focus = "search"
            GuideKeys.handleColumn(key, result)
            return result
        end if
        if key = "options" and current.rows.Count() = 0
            result.action = GuideKeys.action("openSettings")
            return result
        end if
        rowHere = GuideKeys.rowAtFocus(current)
        if rowHere <> invalid and rowHere.kind <> "channel"
            GuideKeys.handleActionRow(key, rowHere, result)
        else if current.focus = "channel"
            GuideKeys.handleChannelCell(key, rowHere, result)
        else
            GuideKeys.handleGrid(key, rowHere, result)
        end if
        if key = "back" then result.action = GuideKeys.backAction(current)
        return result
    end function

    ' The grid: a programme cell.
    sub handleGrid(key as string, rowHere as dynamic, result as object)
        current = result.state
        if key = "up" or key = "down"
            GuideKeys.moveRow(result, GuideKeys.stepOf(key))
        else if GuideKeys.isPageKey(key)
            GuideKeys.moveRow(result, GuideKeys.pageStep(key, GuideKeys.pageRows))
        else if key = "right"
            if current.cellIndex + 1 < current.cellCount then current.cellIndex = current.cellIndex + 1
        else if key = "left"
            if current.cellIndex <= 0
                current.focus = "channel"
            else
                current.cellIndex = current.cellIndex - 1
            end if
        else if key = "OK"
            result.action = GuideKeys.channelAction("play", rowHere)
        else if key = "options"
            ' M7 L5: the channel menu, as OK on the channel cell.
            result.action = GuideKeys.channelAction("channelMenu", rowHere)
        end if
    end sub

    ' The channel cell of the focused row (M6 L8).
    sub handleChannelCell(key as string, rowHere as dynamic, result as object)
        current = result.state
        if key = "up" or key = "down"
            GuideKeys.moveRow(result, GuideKeys.stepOf(key))
        else if GuideKeys.isPageKey(key)
            GuideKeys.moveRow(result, GuideKeys.pageStep(key, GuideKeys.pageRows))
        else if key = "right"
            current.focus = "grid"
        else if key = "left"
            GuideKeys.focusGroups(current)
        else if key = "OK" or key = "options"
            result.action = GuideKeys.channelAction("channelMenu", rowHere)
        end if
    end sub

    ' M7l 8c: My Teams' Choose Teams (and, from step 18, upcoming game) rows, focused as a whole.
    sub handleActionRow(key as string, rowHere as object, result as object)
        current = result.state
        if key = "up" or key = "down"
            GuideKeys.moveRow(result, GuideKeys.stepOf(key))
        else if GuideKeys.isPageKey(key)
            GuideKeys.moveRow(result, GuideKeys.pageStep(key, GuideKeys.pageRows))
        else if key = "OK"
            if rowHere.kind = "upcoming"
                result.action = GuideKeys.channelAction("play", rowHere)
            else
                result.action = GuideKeys.action("openTeamPicker")
            end if
        else if key = "left"
            GuideKeys.focusGroups(current)
        else if key = "right"
            current.focus = "grid"
        end if
    end sub

    ' The group column: Search (focus "search") above the groups (focus "groups", groupFocus).
    sub handleColumn(key as string, result as object)
        current = result.state
        if key = "up" or key = "down"
            GuideKeys.moveInColumn(result, GuideKeys.stepOf(key))
        else if GuideKeys.isPageKey(key)
            GuideKeys.moveInColumn(result, GuideKeys.pageStep(key, GuideKeys.pageGroupRows))
        else if key = "back" or key = "left"
            current.focus = "grid"
        else if key = "options"
            ' Step 13: Settings; the column stays open under it, so Back from Settings comes back here.
            result.action = GuideKeys.action("openSettings")
        else if key = "OK" or key = "right"
            if current.focus = "search"
                ' Focus stays, so closing Search comes back to the Search row.
                result.action = GuideKeys.action("openSearch")
            else if current.groupFocus >= 0 and current.groupFocus < current.groups.Count()
                current.groupIndex = current.groupFocus
                current.rows = GuideKeys.rowsOf(current.lineup, current.groups[current.groupIndex])
                current.row = 0
                current.cellIndex = 0
                current.cellCount = 1
                current.focus = "grid"
                result.action = { type: "groupChanged", group: current.groups[current.groupIndex], groupIndex: current.groupIndex }
            end if
        end if
    end sub

    function setLineup(state as object, built as object) as object
        current = GuideKeys.copyState(state)
        focusedRow = GuideKeys.rowAtFocus(current)
        focusedRowID = GuideKeys.rowID(focusedRow)
        focusedChannelID = ""
        if focusedRow <> invalid
            if focusedRow.kind = "channel" then focusedChannelID = focusedRow.channelID
        end if
        group = GuideKeys.groupName(current.groups, current.groupIndex)
        focusedGroup = invalid
        if current.focus = "groups" then focusedGroup = GuideKeys.groupName(current.groups, current.groupFocus)
        oldRow = current.row
        oldGroupFocus = current.groupFocus

        current.lineup = built
        current.groups = built.groups
        index = -1
        if GuideKeys.isText(group) then index = GuideKeys.textIndex(current.groups, group)
        if index < 0 then index = GuideKeys.defaultGroupIndex(current.groups)
        current.groupIndex = index
        current.rows = GuideKeys.rowsOf(built, GuideKeys.groupName(current.groups, index))
        newRow = -1
        if focusedRowID <> ""
            for i = 0 to current.rows.Count() - 1
                if GuideKeys.rowID(current.rows[i]) = focusedRowID
                    newRow = i
                    exit for
                end if
            end for
        end if
        if newRow < 0 and focusedChannelID <> "" then newRow = GuideKeys.channelRow(current.rows, focusedChannelID)
        if newRow < 0 then newRow = GuideKeys.clamped(oldRow, current.rows.Count())
        current.row = newRow
        if current.focus = "groups"
            groupFocus = -1
            if GuideKeys.isText(focusedGroup) then groupFocus = GuideKeys.textIndex(current.groups, focusedGroup)
            if groupFocus < 0 then groupFocus = GuideKeys.clamped(oldGroupFocus, current.groups.Count())
            current.groupFocus = groupFocus
        else
            current.groupFocus = index
        end if
        return current
    end function

    function jumpTarget(state as object) as dynamic
        if state.rows.Count() = 0 then return invalid
        kind = "grid"
        if state.focus = "channel" then kind = "channel"
        return { row: GuideKeys.clamped(state.row, state.rows.Count()), kind: kind }
    end function

    function pendingFor(target as dynamic, held as dynamic) as dynamic
        if LCase(type(target)) <> "roassociativearray" then return invalid
        if LCase(type(held)) = "roassociativearray"
            if held.row = target.row and held.kind = target.kind then return invalid
        end if
        return target
    end function

    function gridReport(focus as dynamic, pending as dynamic, reported as object, rebuilding = false as boolean) as object
        result = { apply: false, isInput: false, pending: invalid }
        own = false
        if LCase(type(pending)) = "roassociativearray"
            own = pending.kind = reported.kind and pending.row = reported.row
        end if
        if GuideKeys.isText(focus)
            if focus = "groups" or focus = "search" then return result
        end if
        if rebuilding
            result.apply = own
            if not own then result.pending = pending
            return result
        end if
        result.apply = true
        result.isInput = not own
        return result
    end function

    function visibleStart(first as integer, position as integer, count as integer, visible as integer) as integer
        start = first
        if position < start then start = position
        if position >= start + visible then start = position - visible + 1
        highest = count - visible
        if highest < 0 then highest = 0
        if start > highest then start = highest
        if start < 0 then start = 0
        return start
    end function

    ' A row's id, as GuideModel.Row.id: "channel.<id>", "chooseTeams" (step 18 adds "upcoming.…"); "" for none.
    function rowID(row as dynamic) as string
        if row = invalid then return ""
        if row.kind = "channel" then return "channel." + row.channelID
        return row.kind
    end function

    ' value clamped to 0...count - 1 (0 for an empty list).
    function clamped(value as integer, count as integer) as integer
        if value > count - 1 then value = count - 1
        if value < 0 then value = 0
        return value
    end function

    ' LiveTVModel's .close: full screen on the channel; with nothing to return to, the guide stays (D49).
    function backAction(current as object) as object
        if not current.canReturn then return GuideKeys.action("none")
        return { type: "returnToChannel", reload: not current.isPlaying }
    end function

    sub focusGroups(current as object)
        current.focus = "groups"
        current.groupFocus = current.groupIndex
    end sub

    ' M7n L3: a step (±1) past either end wraps to the other end. A page stops at the first or last row and wraps
    ' only from it, so paging never skips past an end unseen. A one-row list stays.
    sub moveRow(result as object, stepSize as integer)
        current = result.state
        count = current.rows.Count()
        if count <= 1 then return
        last = count - 1
        before = current.row
        target = before + stepSize
        if stepSize = 1 or stepSize = -1
            current.row = ((target mod count) + count) mod count
        else if target < 0
            if before = 0 then current.row = last else current.row = 0
        else if target > last
            if before = last then current.row = 0 else current.row = last
        else
            current.row = target
        end if
        if (stepSize > 0 and current.row < before) or (stepSize < 0 and current.row > before) then result.wrapped = true
    end sub

    ' The group column loops like the rows: position 0 is Search, 1… the groups. Without groups Search stays.
    sub moveInColumn(result as object, stepSize as integer)
        current = result.state
        groupCount = current.groups.Count()
        if groupCount = 0 then return
        position = 0
        if current.focus = "groups" then position = current.groupFocus + 1
        last = groupCount
        target = position + stepSize
        newPosition = target
        if stepSize = 1 or stepSize = -1
            newPosition = ((target mod (last + 1)) + last + 1) mod (last + 1)
        else if target < 0
            if position = 0 then newPosition = last else newPosition = 0
        else if target > last
            if position = last then newPosition = 0 else newPosition = last
        end if
        if (stepSize > 0 and newPosition < position) or (stepSize < 0 and newPosition > position) then result.wrapped = true
        if newPosition = 0
            current.focus = "search"
        else
            current.focus = "groups"
            current.groupFocus = newPosition - 1
        end if
    end sub

    function rowAtFocus(current as object) as dynamic
        if current.row < 0 or current.row >= current.rows.Count() then return invalid
        return current.rows[current.row]
    end function

    function channelAction(kind as string, row as dynamic) as object
        if row = invalid or not GuideKeys.isText(row.channelID) or row.channelID = "" then return GuideKeys.action("none")
        return { type: kind, channelID: row.channelID }
    end function

    function isPageKey(key as string) as boolean
        return key = "rewind" or key = "fastforward" or key = "channelup" or key = "channeldown"
    end function

    function pageStep(key as string, size as integer) as integer
        if key = "rewind" or key = "channelup" then return -size
        return size
    end function

    function stepOf(key as string) as integer
        if key = "up" then return -1
        return 1
    end function

    function action(kind as string) as object
        return { type: kind }
    end function

    ' A new state object; a missing or mistyped field reads as its default.
    function copyState(state as dynamic) as object
        result = {
            focus: "grid",
            lineup: { groups: [], visibleChannels: [], favoritesGroupChannels: [], teams: [] },
            groups: [],
            groupIndex: 0,
            groupFocus: 0,
            rows: [],
            row: 0,
            cellIndex: 0,
            cellCount: 1,
            canReturn: false,
            isPlaying: false
        }
        if LCase(type(state)) <> "roassociativearray" then return result
        for each field in ["focus", "lineup", "groups", "groupIndex", "groupFocus", "rows", "row", "cellIndex", "cellCount", "canReturn", "isPlaying"]
            value = state[field]
            if value <> invalid and GuideKeys.sameKind(value, result[field]) then result[field] = value
        end for
        if result.focus <> "grid" and result.focus <> "channel" and result.focus <> "groups" and result.focus <> "search" then result.focus = "grid"
        if result.cellCount < 1 then result.cellCount = 1
        if result.cellIndex >= result.cellCount then result.cellIndex = result.cellCount - 1
        if result.cellIndex < 0 then result.cellIndex = 0
        return result
    end function

    ' The first group that isn't My Teams nor Antenna, else Antenna, else 0.
    function defaultGroupIndex(groups as object) as integer
        for i = 0 to groups.Count() - 1
            if groups[i] <> Lineup.teamsGroup and groups[i] <> Lineup.antennaGroup then return i
        end for
        antenna = GuideKeys.textIndex(groups, Lineup.antennaGroup)
        if antenna >= 0 then return antenna
        return 0
    end function

    function groupName(groups as object, index as integer) as dynamic
        if index < 0 or index >= groups.Count() then return invalid
        return groups[index]
    end function

    function channelRow(rows as object, id as string) as integer
        for i = 0 to rows.Count() - 1
            if rows[i].kind = "channel" and rows[i].channelID = id then return i
        end for
        return -1
    end function

    function textIndex(list as object, value as string) as integer
        for i = 0 to list.Count() - 1
            if list[i] = value then return i
        end for
        return -1
    end function

    function sameKind(a as dynamic, b as dynamic) as boolean
        return GuideKeys.kindOf(a) = GuideKeys.kindOf(b)
    end function

    function kindOf(value as dynamic) as string
        kind = LCase(type(value))
        if kind = "rostring" then return "string"
        if kind = "roint" or kind = "rointeger" or kind = "integer" or kind = "longinteger" or kind = "rolonginteger" or kind = "float" or kind = "rofloat" or kind = "double" or kind = "rodouble" then return "number"
        if kind = "roboolean" then return "boolean"
        return kind
    end function

    function isKey(key as dynamic) as boolean
        if not GuideKeys.isText(key) then return false
        for each known in ["up", "down", "left", "right", "OK", "back", "options", "replay", "play", "rewind", "fastforward", "channelup", "channeldown"]
            if key = known then return true
        end for
        return false
    end function

    function isText(value as dynamic) as boolean
        kind = LCase(type(value))
        return kind = "string" or kind = "rostring"
    end function

end namespace
